        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-696",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "MISSING MAC-BEFORE-DECRYPT ORDERING in JWE AES-CBC-HMAC: in `_decrypt_and_auth` (jose/jwe.py), the ciphertext is decrypted AND PKCS7-unpadded at line 239 (`plaintext = encryption_key.decrypt(cipher_text, iv, aad, auth_tag)`) and only AFTERWARDS is the HMAC authentication tag compared, at line 240 (`auth_tag != auth_tag_check`). For the `A*CBC-HS*` enc values the callee is CryptographyAESKey.decrypt (jose/backends/cryptography_backend.py:490), whose non-GCM branch runs `decryptor.update/finalize` (lines 507-508) and then `PKCS7(...).unpadder().update(padded_plain_text)` (lines 509-510) with no MAC check of its own. A PKCS7 unpadding failure therefore raises a different error than the `JWEError(\"Invalid JWE Auth Tag\")` raised at line 241, giving an attacker a padding oracle (Vaudenay/Lucky-13 class) against attacker-submitted JWE tokens. The required control -- verify the HMAC tag over (aad||iv||ciphertext||al) BEFORE performing any CBC decryption or unpadding -- is absent.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived independently from source. In _decrypt_and_auth (jose/jwe.py:230-243) the AES-CBC ciphertext is decrypted and PKCS7-unpadded at line 239 and the HMAC tag is only compared afterwards at lines 240-241, so attacker-controlled ciphertext is processed by the unpadder before any authentication. The callee for A*CBC-HS* enc values is CryptographyAESKey.decrypt (jose/backends/cryptography_backend.py:490); its non-GCM else-branch (504-511) runs decryptor.update/finalize then PKCS7 unpadder.update/finalize with no MAC check of its own (only the GCM branch at 495-503 authenticates). constants.py:67 confirms A128CBC_HS256/A192CBC_HS384/A256CBC_HS512 route into the HMAC_AUTH_TAG branch. Critically, _auth_tag (jwe.py:571-574) computes the MAC over aad+iv+ciphertext+al, i.e. Encrypt-then-MAC per RFC 7518 5.2.2, so the tag is fully verifiable BEFORE decryption, and auth_tag_check is already available at line 232 -- the fix is a trivial reorder of 240-241 above 239. This proves the missing MAC-before-decrypt ordering is a real defect, not an inherent constraint. The code also violates its own stated requirement in the comment at jwe.py:175-176 (\"rejecting the input without emitting any decrypted output if the JWE Authentication Tag is incorrect\"). Reachability verified in source: public jwe.decrypt() (line 60) calls _decrypt_and_auth at line 178 with no prior tag verification anywhere in lines 79-178; the graph independently reports reachable_from_entry=true, hop_distance=1 for lines 178/232/239/240/241. Severity held at MEDIUM rather than HIGH because a padding failure and a tag mismatch both ultimately surface as JWEError (backend rewraps at cryptography_backend.py:514-515, jwe.py:181-182 rewraps again) with differing messages, so the strength of the padding oracle depends on whether the embedding application exposes the distinct message/behavior; an application returning a uniform error leaks only through the weaker timing channel. Exploit-reference check could not corroborate: the Metasploit corpus returned \"exploit corpus unavailable: not indexed\", so no module/CVE/version comparison was possible and it contributed nothing to this verdict either way."
          },
